{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>A thousand.</b> In construct with one of them, and it is a descriptor for a leader, and the meaning is that a leader who has a thousand men will flee from the rebuke of one man." "<b>You shall flee.</b> All of you." "<b>Like a mast.</b> A hint that a few of the many will remain, and what seems correct to me is that the meaning refers to those gathered among the remnant in Jerusalem who did not go down to Egypt."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:01.242657322Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}